    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "it just feels so heavy. talking about this makes me feel like i'm drifting into that same gray space. like, if elias's choice is the only honest way to find symmetry, then maybe the \"rest\" you mentioned isn't just for the book. it's like, if you're already feeling that emptiness, isn't it just more exhausting to keep pretending there's a reason to stay in the struggle?",
